WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.875
Model and runtime choices are security and operations decisions,

00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:05.400
not just engineering preferences.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.475
Model size, model capability, quantization, context window, latency,

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.880
hardware requirements, memory needs, licensing,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.300
and supportability all affect whether a system can be safely operated.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.900
The best model for a workflow is not always the largest or newest model.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.975
It is the model whose capability, cost, control, and reliability fit the job.

00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:25.730
A smaller model may be faster, cheaper, easier to isolate,

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.695
and good enough for a focused workflow.

00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:31.500
A larger model may be helpful for complex reasoning or broader language tasks,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.500
but it may require more expensive hardware, stricter monitoring,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.090
and clearer usage controls.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.300
Quantization and runtime settings can reduce resource demands,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.300
but they may also affect output quality, latency, and evaluation requirements.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.500
The runtime determines real system behavior.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.800
It controls how requests are accepted, how sessions are managed, how context is assembled,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.475
whether outputs stream, what rate limits apply, and how usage is logged.

00:00:53.475 --> 00:00:56.885
Local model runners, inference servers, private endpoints, gateways,

00:00:56.885 --> 00:01:00.690
and orchestration layers each create different operational responsibilities.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.795
Tool access deserves special attention.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:07.360
Tools let an AI system search, read, write, call APIs, create tickets, run workflows,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.300
or interact with internal systems.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.540
A private model with broad tools can still create serious operational risk if permissions

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.510
are unclear.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:18.470
Sovereign AI requires deliberate runtime decisions, scoped tools, monitored usage,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.050
and approval patterns for sensitive actions.

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.480
Downloading a model is not the same thing as designing a controlled AI system.
